# Cloudflare Pages SPA fallback.
#
# This application is a single-page app: React Router owns every path, and only index.html exists on
# disk. Without this rule Pages serves the built assets and returns its own 404 for anything else,
# so the site works when you click through it and breaks the moment anyone reloads on /clients,
# follows a link into /billing, or opens a password-reset link — which is every path that actually
# matters for a new user.
#
# The 200 is the important part. A 301 or 302 would change the address bar and lose the path, so
# React Router would never see it; a rewrite keeps the URL and hands index.html to the browser,
# which lets the router resolve the route it was asked for.
#
# Vite copies everything in public/ into dist/, which is what Pages deploys.
/*  /index.html  200
